          "type": "turn",
          "question": "How often do they recheck it?",
          "answer": "The recommended frequency for rechecking blood pressure varies based on individual circumstances, particularly whether a person has been diagnosed with hypertension or not.\n\nFor adults diagnosed with high blood pressure (hypertension), the general guidance suggests:\n- Monthly reviews until the target blood pressure is reached.\n- After reaching a stable target, rechecks can be conducted every three to six months.\n\nThis information is based on guidelines from major cardiology societies regarding hypertension management, found in the document titled \"Hypertension: when treatment starts and which options are first-line.\"\n\nIf you have specific concerns or conditions regarding blood pressure management, it would be best to discuss these with a healthcare professional.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
